# Generated output. `bun start` runs `bun format` first, so anything prettier
# cannot parse in here takes the whole dev server down with exit code 2 — which
# is how a doc heading containing a literal `<tosi-ensemble>` tag stopped the
# site from booting at all.
docs/
docs.last-good/
demo/docs.json
node_modules/

# Build output. `dist/` is gitignored and regenerated on every build, so
# formatting it is 70 files of churn that no human reads and that `--check`
# can never keep green — which is how a formatting gate ends up disabled and
# real drift in hand-written code goes unnoticed.
dist/

# Test-runner output, both gitignored.
test-results/
playwright-report/
.browser-tests.json

# Pre-release review reports are filed VERBATIM, as the record of what was
# found and what was not fixed. Reformatting an agent's report edits evidence.
reviews/

# ⚠️ ONE EXCEPTION, AND IT IS THE WRONG ONE — tosijs-ui#165.
# The doc system rewrites this file's `<!-- toc -->` block on every build and
# emits it without the blank line Prettier's markdown formatter always inserts,
# so `format` and `build` undo each other and a `--check` gate can never stay
# green. Ignoring it means the repo's one hand-written doc PAGE is the only
# file the formatter does not check; remove this line the moment #165 lands.
editor.md

# Copied UNCHANGED from tosijs-coding-practices/templates — the rollout's adoption
# check is byte-identity with the template, so the formatter must not touch it.
.github/workflows/publish.yml
